     5  ## iPhone announces shared-normal-tabs-v3 and gates its tab writes — 29 September 2026
     6
     7  Owner-authorized mobile-lane session; commit `2658cfe8` on branch `mobile/ios-shared-tab-capability` in the
     8  worktree `../AhoiBrowser-ios-capability` (base `e0cb5086`), not pushed.
     9  Cause: the real-device run
    10  ([evidence](../artifacts/sync-acceptance/real-device-20260929/),
    11  [coordination](ACTIVE_SYNC_COORDINATION.md)) showed the Mac correctly
    12  withholding its Page/Presence writes, because the iPhone never wrote its own
    13  capability record, and the iPhone wrote tabs without checking its peers.
    14
    15  - **Announcement** (`SharedTabWriterGate.swift`,
    16    `LocalFirstRepository.publishLocalSharedTabCapability`). This mirrors
    17    desktop `PublishLocalCapability`: one Format-3 `DeviceCapabilityRecord`,
    18    entity 12, id UUIDv5 `ahoi:sync:capability:v1:<device>`, models `[3]`.
    19    It is written after the own Device record, first as a control announcement
    20    with `features: []`. It declares `shared-normal-tabs-v3` once
    21    `MobileSharedTabIntentBinding` has wired native capture and projection
    22    (`activateSharedTabNativeSupport`). It is never downgraded, and it is never
    23    written for a retired or tombstoned own Device or a tombstoned
    24    declaration. `performSync` publishes it before `syncNow`, and the
    25    local-snapshot reseed carries it. There is no withdrawal path, as on
    26    desktop (ADR 0009: local wiring gaps are not a format downgrade; peers
    27    ignore a retired Device's declaration).
    28  - **Writer gate.** After every completed bounded pass,
    29    `refreshSharedTabWriterGate` feeds `SharedTabCapabilityReadiness` from the
    30    snapshot Devices and declarations and from provider acknowledgements. A new
    31    transport query `isRecordAcknowledged` requires a savedRecords
    32    system-field receipt and no pending save. The semantics match desktop
    33    `SharedTabState()`: every non-retired, non-tombstoned Device needs a valid
    34    declaration with the feature; a declaration for an unknown Device blocks;
    35    and the own Device and capability records must be acknowledged. While the
    36    gate is closed, the bridge keeps this device's Presences and the Pages
    37    written by the shared-tab paths (capture, intent, close, saved page) out of
    38    transport, including in `enqueueLocalSnapshot`. Opening the gate reseeds
    39    that backlog. If only the own acknowledgements are missing, one extra pass
    40    runs per runtime generation. Device, Session and Workspace records are not
    41    gated. Generic companion tree edits (rename, move, delete in the Workspace
    42    UI) keep their old path. The desktop gates its native tree journal as well;
    43    this difference is left for the owner to decide.
    44  - **Tests (not run yet)**: `SharedTabWriterGateTests` (golden parity with
    45    `device_capability_iphone` from `sync_wire_v3.json`: id, key sets, feature,
    46    models, decode through the peer path; announcement rules; gate open and
    47    closed, including the Mac-without-declaration case, retired and offline
    48    peers, unknown device, missing acks, native wiring and sync; transport
    49    withholding and reseed; model wiring end to end on the in-memory
    50    transport). The convergence relay, the CloudKit domain E2E and the
    51    single-device visible UI projection open the gate explicitly. See the
    52    report line below for the run status.
    53  - **Owner verification on the iPhone.** Rebuild `AhoiMobile-CloudKitDevelopment`
    54    / `CloudKitDevelopment` from `2658cfe8` or later with the **same** scope
    55    settings as [ios/README.md](../artifacts/sync-acceptance/real-device-20260929/ios/README.md)
    56    (scope `23855a90-…`, zone, subscription and Keychain account unchanged).
    57    Install over the existing app with `devicectl` and do not reset its data.
    58    Open it and run Settings "Jetzt synchronisieren" once or twice. No Mac
    59    rebuild is needed.
    60  - **Expected Mac readback** (scoped `sync-format3.sqlite`, read from a copy):
    61    two `deviceCapability` rows (entity 12), the Mac's and the iPhone's. The
    62    iPhone row has `features=["shared-normal-tabs-v3"]` and device_id equal to
    63    the iPhone Device row. After that the Mac gate opens and a new capture
    64    writes a `treeNode` (entity 2) Page and a `deviceTab` (entity 4) Presence
    65    for `https://example.com/?ahoi-sync-mac-20260929T112130Z`, if that Mac tab
    66    is still open. The iPhone receive journey should then find it under
    67    "Geräte-Tabs". Two preconditions: the Mac's own declaration must carry the
    68    feature (the iPhone received a Mac `deviceCapability` in run 6, but its
    69    feature list was not read out), and the zone must hold no stale active
    70    Device without a declaration. Either one keeps both gates closed by design.
